      "attributes": [
        {
          "doc_text": " Provides intentionally-saturating arithmetic on `T`.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            237,
            293
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            294,
            297
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Operations like `+` on `u32` values are intended to never overflow,",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            298,
            369
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " and in some debug configurations overflow is detected and results",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            370,
            439
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " in a panic. While most arithmetic falls into this category, some",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            440,
            508
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " code explicitly expects and relies upon saturating arithmetic.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            509,
            575
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            576,
            579
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " Saturating arithmetic can be achieved either through methods like",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            580,
            649
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `saturating_add`, or through the `Saturating<T>` type, which says that",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            650,
            724
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " all standard arithmetic operations on the underlying value are",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            725,
            791
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " intended to have saturating semantics.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            792,
            834
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            835,
            838
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " The underlying value can be retrieved through the `.0` index of the",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            839,
            910
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " `Saturating` tuple.",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            911,
            934
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            935,
            938
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " # Examples",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            939,
            953
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            954,
            957
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " ```",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            958,
            965
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " use std::num::Saturating;",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            966,
            995
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": "",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            996,
            999
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let max = Saturating(u32::MAX);",
          "path": "doc",
          "range": [
            1000,
            1035
          ],
          "style": "outer"
        },
        {
          "doc_text": " let one = Saturating(1u32);",
          "path": "doc",
